<title>UK: Ward drops after bid talks ended.</title>
<headline>Ward drops after bid talks ended.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ward Holdings Plc shares tumbled 28.6 percent on Wednesday after the British housebuilder said after Tuesday's close it had broken off talks with potential bidders.</p>
<p>The stock was down 20p at 50 by 0756 GMT. Ward said it had decided that discussions being held were unlikely to lead to an offer which adequately reflected its value, and would instead pay a special 1p dividend.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
